WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
Open two Gospels at the same
saying of Jesus, about divorce.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.620
Mark gives no exception.

3
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.460
Matthew adds one.

4
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:13.640
Today, Catholic, Orthodox and many Protestant
churches handle remarriage in different

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.670
ways.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.560
Christians also read the
Bible's words on suffering,

7
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.740
and on leaders, in sharply different ways.

8
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.370
If Christians share one Bible, why
do they read it so differently?

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.350
In this mission, you'll explore how texts
from Job to the cross have shaped Christian

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.180
thinking about suffering.

11
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.200
Then you'll weigh up a live debate: what
makes a leader in a faith community,

12
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.920
and who may lead?

13
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out why one
Bible is read in so many ways.
